                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a cute little tower defense game, but far too short and too repetitive to be of interest. The animation is nice, the gameplay is simple but not challenging or inventive, and there is no variety to the levels. Three planets, about six levels each, and most of the levels take under three minutes. Every level can be beaten easily on the first try. (The only battle I lost was because I was trying a stunt of using only the weakest units, which didn't work out so well.) Even playing for the \"Perfectionist\" achievement (five stars for every level) will only take a couple of hours. There was only one level that required more than a few tries to get the five-star score. All but two of the achievements are also trivial. The first is \"Upgrade a unit to level 10,\" which takes a long time just because you have to repeat the same battle many times in order to afford the upgrades. The other is \"beat the game on the highest difficulty,\" which I'm not going to bother with, because replaying it and making it harder doesn't make it more enjoyable. Spent my couple bucks, played through it in an evening, uninstalled it.",
